  "title": "The Second Time Through",
  "subtitle": "\"I died at sixty-eight in a war I'd spent fifty years trying to stop. I woke up at seventeen in my parents' kitchen in Wichita with the System asking me, politely, what class I would like this time.\"",
  "penName": "Owen Kalb",
  "genre": "regressionTimeloop",
  "hook": "I died at sixty-eight in a refugee camp in what used to be Denver. I had spent fifty years of my first life trying to prevent the war that had finally killed me. The System came to me in death and asked if I would like to try again. I said yes. I woke in my parents' kitchen in Wichita, Kansas, at seventeen years old, in September of the year before the first attack. My mother was alive. My sister was alive. The System asked me what class I wanted. I thought for a long time before I answered.",
